{
  "name": "AI Guest Messaging Assistant for Vacation Rentals",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 🏠 AI GUEST MESSAGING ASSISTANT FOR VACATION RENTALS\n**What it does:** Webhook receives inbound guest messages (Airbnb / Booking.com via channel-manager or PMS webhook, email via an IMAP-to-webhook bridge) → AI classifies the message and drafts a reply → safe FAQs (WiFi, check-in/out, house rules, amenities) get an instant auto-reply → sensitive topics (refunds, complaints, access codes, safety) escalate to the host on Telegram with a suggested draft.\n\n**You'll need:**\n- OpenAI API key (platform.openai.com)\n- Google Sheets OAuth2 credential\n- Telegram bot token + your chat ID (@BotFather → /newbot)\n- A channel-manager/PMS (Hostaway, Lodgify, Guesty…) or OTA webhook forwarding inbound guest messages to the workflow's webhook URL\n\n**Status flow in Sheets:** `NEW` → `PROCESSING` → `AUTO_REPLIED` / `ESCALATED`",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 6200,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "e2e6d4ac-640e-4eeb-9434-95a602de40be",
      "name": "STICKY — Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -180
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 1 — Inbound guest message\nWebhook receives the guest message from your PMS/channel-manager/email bridge → normalize channel, property, guest name and message text.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 1320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b5002eaf-5f48-479b-8135-28143fc25be1",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 2 — Log to Google Sheets\nAppend a row with status `NEW`, then flip it to `PROCESSING` while the AI works.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 880,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b9a96d70-0b32-4fd4-aa68-2ddede17f66b",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        940,
        160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 3 — AI classify + draft\nAI Agent reads the message with property context and returns structured output: intent, confidence 0–1, auto_reply_allowed, draft_reply, escalation_reason.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "f582168c-0192-4e20-b485-b3e8636f6b07",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1840,
        160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 4 — Safe auto-reply branch\n`auto_reply_allowed = true` AND confidence ≥ threshold → POST the draft to your reply endpoint → sheet flips to `AUTO_REPLIED` → host gets a Telegram summary.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 1420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b5445675-dd24-445f-bf8c-3a9f343a164c",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2220,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 5 — Escalation branch\nRefunds, complaints, access codes, safety, schedule changes or low confidence → sheet flips to `ESCALATED` → host gets a Telegram alert with the AI's suggested draft. The host replies manually.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 1420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "fedab551-44b4-4ca3-8339-32af938901b5",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2220,
        590
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## STEP 6 — Acknowledge webhook\nBoth branches merge → return `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` to the caller.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "6551110c-7219-4879-9364-a94b1161f385",
      "name": "STICKY — STEP 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
